NOTICE.md --- Text
11 11 The README hero was generated for this project. It is illustrative artwork, not hardware evidence. Browser screenshots use synthetic local fixtures. No external fonts, customer records or stock photographs are included. See docs/assets/README.md.
12 12
13 13 HeavenKey 0.3 uses @simplewebauthn/browser 14.0.0 as its browser ceremony adapter. The MIT license and Matthew Miller copyright notice are preserved in docs/licenses/simplewebauthn-browser-MIT.txt and included in every generated browser bundle. It introduces no transitive runtime dependency. The exact package SHA-512 is pinned in bun.lock; dependency decisions and source links are recorded in docs/DONORS.md.
   14
   15 The 0.7 source uses keyring 3.6.3 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) for the platform credential store and OpenSSL for an authenticated issuer envelope. The Linux native build uses the vendored libdbus library through libdbus-sys; libdbus is used under its Academic Free License 2.1 option. The packaging script preserves vendor/dbus/COPYING and includes the unmodified libdbus-sys source archive alongside MPL-licensed sources. Standalone GPL-only libdbus tools are not built as HeavenKey application components. cbor-x and happy-dom are development/test dependencies, not part of the browser production bundle.
   16
   17 The seven 0.7 instruction SVGs are original, reproducible schematic illustrations generated by scripts/illustrate_guides.py. They are not browser screenshots or hardware evidence.

